/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Problem Statement: Managers across various industries, including life sciences, healthcare, manufacturing, and warehousing, often face the challenge of choosing between increasing labor costs for repetitive tasks or diverting skilled staff from their primary responsibilities. High turnover rates among low-skill, part-time workers lead to ongoing labor and training expenses, while using experienced staff for menial tasks lowers productivity, morale, and focus on high-value work, ultimately increasing human effort and causing burnout.)
/E (Problem Statement: Managers across various industries, including life sciences, healthcare, manufacturing, and warehousing, often face the challenge of choosing between increasing labor costs for repetitive tasks or diverting skilled staff from their primary responsibilities. High turnover rates among low-skill, part-time workers lead to ongoing labor and training expenses, while using experienced staff for menial tasks lowers productivity, morale, and focus on high-value work, ultimately increasing human effort and causing burnout.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [0]
